THE THREE MISSES, CAUSE MEASURED (not re-pinned -- resume-pending SS6)
  Localised: 994 of 1,014 and 1,405 of 1,405 beyond-band _msn texels sit on the
  NORTH border; distances 4,5,6,7 only; every other border reaches exactly 3.
  --dump-land over cells x=-24..-17 says Bethesda's own landscape disagrees
  across exactly ONE shared vertex row in this neighbourhood -- y=31 | y=32, by
  1..9 VHGT units (8..72 world units). Seams y=23|24, y=27|28, y=32|33 and both
  east seams read 0, i.e. exact agreement.
  So lodgenTerrainFillRing's documented south->north order lets the y=32 cell
  overwrite the shared row, changing the chunk's OWN boundary grid row where the
  clamp did not. Reach follows arithmetically: a texel at distance t reads
  heights at t+-4 texels through a bilinear tap, so grid index -1 is read out to
  t=3 (the passing borders) and grid index 0 out to t=7 (the north border).
  The pre-registered band of 4 counted the central difference's 128-unit step
  but not the bilinear tap's own 128-unit footprint, and assumed the ring could
  only touch points OUTSIDE the chunk.
  The 16 _data texels are exactly one 4x4 BC block at d=76..79: chgt copies the
  ring's middle, whose north boundary row moved, and wetness is a flow
  accumulation over that whole grid -- a global operator. That is owed item 2 of
  the lane's own report, not a new finding.

